From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AzCore/Script: lua_newstate signature compat for Lua 5.5

Lua 5.5 (released 2026 ahead of Fedora 45's debut in rawhide) added a
required third parameter to `lua_newstate`:

  Lua 5.4:  lua_State *lua_newstate(lua_Alloc f, void *ud);
  Lua 5.5:  lua_State *lua_newstate(lua_Alloc f, void *ud, unsigned int seed);

The new `seed` parameter randomizes Lua's string-table hash seed to
mitigate hash-collision DoS. Passing `0` disables randomization (engine
asset-build / scripting workflows do not consume untrusted strings at
the rate where collision attacks are realistic; the hash seeding is
still applied internally for fixed-table operations).

Caught on COPR build 10436540 (o3de-experimental 14-pack, fedora-rawhide
chroot, 2026-05-08): rawhide's lua-devel-5.5.x failed compilation of
`Code/Framework/AzCore/AzCore/Script/ScriptContext.cpp:4359`:

  error: no matching function for call to 'lua_newstate'
  /usr/include/lua.h:163:21: note: candidate function not viable:
  requires 3 arguments, but 2 were provided

Same source builds cleanly on F44 (lua 5.4.8). The `LUA_VERSION_NUM`
preprocessor symbol is documented public Lua API (defined in luaconf.h);
guarding on `>= 505` keeps the patch behavior-preserving for Lua 5.4
consumers while letting Lua 5.5+ compile.

This patch is independent of the `system_lua` bcond -- the engine
ScriptContext invokes `lua_newstate` regardless of whether Lua comes
from the bundled `Lua-5.4.4-rev1-linux` package or from system
`lua-devel`. With `--with system_lua` ON: the rebuilt engine links
against whatever Lua the distro ships (5.4 on F44, 5.5 on rawhide).
With `--with system_lua` OFF: the bundled Lua is 5.4 so the
`#if` branch always evaluates false and behavior is unchanged.

This is sibling to Patch0008 (drop the redundant `<Lua/lobject.h>`
include in the same file) but addresses a separate concern: API
signature drift across major Lua versions, vs. that patch's
internal-header-cleanup goal.

Worth pitching upstream: every distro that follows rawhide will
eventually ship Lua 5.5 (Debian unstable, Alpine edge, Arch). The
fix is small, behavior-preserving, and version-gated.

Signed-off-by: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
---
--- a/Code/Framework/AzCore/AzCore/Script/ScriptContext.cpp
+++ b/Code/Framework/AzCore/AzCore/Script/ScriptContext.cpp
@@ -4356,7 +4356,11 @@
                     {
                         allocator = &m_luaAllocator;
                     }
+#if LUA_VERSION_NUM >= 505
+                    m_lua = lua_newstate(&LuaMemoryHook, allocator, 0);
+#else
                     m_lua = lua_newstate(&LuaMemoryHook, allocator);
+#endif
                     AZ_Assert(m_lua, "Failed to create new LUA state!");
                 }

